# 基本図形編集の用紙枠設定を、デスクトップの図形編集とプロセスの図形編集で同じに使う
# (design 11.3, 17.13), for tools/ui_run.py. A figure of one rectangle and two zigzag lines
# (mkbig fig 1 2 0) opened at 100,100 to 900,700. 用紙枠設定 is the second row of 書式/印刷's
# own menu. The menu opens with the item chosen last on the pointer's row, the rows 20 apart,
# an item's own menu beside it with its first row on the item's: in the desktop's figure
# 閉じる (書式/印刷 seven rows under); in the process's, the system's menus remembering,
# 書式/印刷. The panel (用紙, its list, 縦 横, 余白 上 下 左 右, 割付 片面 見開き, ヘッダ/フッタ,
# 標準設定, 取消, 設定) is kept on the screen to be compared; B4 chosen from the list, 15 typed
# after the 0 of 上, 見開き, 設定. Saved, record 0 comes out the same, byte for byte, its
# <paper> and <docmargin> written ahead of the figure. Both put the panel in the middle of the
# screen (397,232), its parts in the same places within it, so the presses are the same.
# Keys: '1' 1e, '5' 22; Ctrl+S 16 01, Ctrl+E 08 01.
# the desktop's figure editor opened by open, whatever the program object says (figproc kernel)
figproc kernel
mkbig fig 1 2 0
open big
waitwin 画用紙 600
sync 600
wait 500
click 600 400 1
wait 500
move 610 540
wait 400
move 720 540
wait 150
move 720 560
wait 300
click 720 560
wait 1500
shot ppc_k_panel
click 495 310
wait 300
click 560 440
wait 300
key 1e
wait 150
key 22
wait 300
click 595 505
wait 300
shot ppc_k_set
click 815 537
wait 800
sync 600
key 16 01
sync 600
sum show
keep kernel
key 08 01
sync 600
wait 500
mkbig fig 1 2 0
logmark
pfig big
expectsincein 60 figure: opened 画用紙 shapes 3
wait 800
logmark
click 600 400 1
expectsince figure: menu
wait 500
move 610 400
wait 400
move 720 400
wait 150
move 720 420
wait 300
click 720 420
expectsince figure: paper panel open
wait 1500
shot ppc_p_panel
click 495 310
wait 300
click 560 440
wait 300
key 1e
wait 150
key 22
wait 300
click 595 505
wait 300
shot ppc_p_set
logmark
click 815 537
expectsince figure: paper panel answered 1
wait 500
logmark
key 16 01
expectsince figure: saved (0)
sum show
same kernel
key 08 01
expect figure: closed
